#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:5
#: 9aa78553388f4a688b90270de8fd0e9f
msgid "Guided mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:7
#: cad6452bc1c4415eb12182f00fde6200
msgid "Guided mode is designed to allow ground stations or :ref:`companion computers <common-companion-computers>` to control the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:10
#: 211edc34211a4f1f86cd085c17e176de
msgid "Sending Commands from the Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:12
#: 5bca009a8d9d4f02bed6e1fc1592ee56
msgid "Most ground stations support commanding the vehicle to drive to a location specified by clicking on the map.  If using the Mission Planner:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:14
#: 0b3e0a44e2f24e8eba427f51a235dcf9
msgid "connect to the vehicle with a :ref:`telemetry radio <common-telemetry-landingpage>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:15
#: 5bdeceebe7ad40eda94ae3c00ab76405
msgid "from the Flight Data screen, right-mouse-button click on the map and select \"Fly To Here\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:16
#: 5d0f51a3b1f44ae793f2102531a14181
msgid "the vehicle will switch to Guided mode and attempted to drive to the location specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:17
#: c3d185c4d53646b3b010acf75f5e5acb
msgid "once at the destination it will hold position if a surface vehicle, or loiter/circle around the destination if it is a boat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:22
#: f51d572155de414e9c52009900b9fe42
msgid "The ground station will normally set the vehicle to Guided mode before the target destination is sent meaning it is not necessary to set up Guided mode on the :ref:`transmitter mode switch <common-rc-transmitter-flight-mode-configuration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:25
#: fbf2e41f566640239afdd0717dd7a59a
msgid "Speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:27
#: eebaeb40f69f430ba94fb80fcf6c5267
msgid "While the vehicle is travelling, the user can increase the vehicle's speed by raising the transmitter's throttle stick to between 75% and 100%.  At 75% the vehicle will remain at it's configured speed (i.e. :ref:`WP_SPEED <WP_SPEED>` or :ref:`CRUISE <CRUISE_SPEED>` if :ref:`WP_SPEED <WP_SPEED>` is zero, versions of Rover after 3.5.1 use only :ref:`WP_SPEED <WP_SPEED>`), this linearly increases to the vehicle's maximum speed as the pilot's throttle stick reaches 100%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guided-mode.rst:30
